{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"id\":31783,\"title\":\"Worst Cooks in America\",\"tagline\":\"\",\"overview\":\"12 to 16 contestants with poor cooking skills are taken through an eight-week culinary boot camp, to earn a cash prize of $25,000. The recruits are trained on the various basic cooking techniques including: baking, knife skills, temperature, seasoning and preparation. The final challenge is to cook a restaurant quality three-course meal for three food critics.\",\"posterPath\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/vE3uKy2AGHQAyDLJ3nR08zpkRJ0.jpg\",\"backdropPath\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/zPaCuvPr2OreS29xpUtWAoK2gQ4.jpg\",\"youtubeBackdrop\":null,\"anilistBanner\":null,\"rating\":6.6,\"voteCount\":31,\"year\":2010,\"genres\":[\"Reality\",\"Comedy\"],\"status\":\"Returning Series\",\"type\":\"tv\",\"totalSeasons\":30,\"totalEpisodes\":226,\"createdBy\":[],\"networks\":[\"Food Network\"],\"countries\":[{\"code\":\"US\",\"name\":\"United States of America\"}],\"lastAirDate\":\"2026-02-01\",\"cast\":[{\"id\":1230170,\"name\":\"Anne Burrell\",\"character\":\"Self - Host\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/zGc4ehyRI3sNjmjEM3NHAueLq0K.jpg\"}],\"trailers\":[{\"key\":\"KmxFxC8QuTk\",\"name\":\"Official Trailer\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"},{\"key\":\"Y6euQGKUcJs\",\"name\":\"Official Trailer\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"},{\"key\":\"WeJtdDaw5f0\",\"name\":\"Official Trailer\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"}],\"similar\":[{\"id\":94653,\"title\":\"Taskmaster Norway\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/moZMbtcK2W2P35vemwW7xyBFLaf.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"year\":2019,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.40588235294117647,\"_genreOverlap\":2},{\"id\":61042,\"title\":\"American Grilled\",\"poster\":null,\"rating\":5,\"year\":2014,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.23559322033898306,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":61086,\"title\":\"Food Fighters\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/kNpgK66jsCzaRGo0fzYcpBxrVM1.jpg\",\"rating\":2,\"year\":2014,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.23157894736842105,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":128297,\"title\":\"Paik Class (Baek Jong Won's Class)\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/1NT98uDoSl95B17mPlHKmkGpUeh.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"year\":2021,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.22359550561797753,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":60892,\"title\":\"Chopped Canada\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/bk0NJE6MhEGdzghhZdVu6vr0KOc.jpg\",\"rating\":5,\"year\":2014,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.22258064516129034,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":743,\"title\":\"Beauty and the Geek\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/83lFzXescQFVzVkUmjwg1zqeMlm.jpg\",\"rating\":7.5,\"year\":2005,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.22210526315789475,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":312276,\"title\":\"Honeysuckle\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/oHVCfozOhlXRZN8lPkhSIN5Z2Mt.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"year\":2022,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.2210526315789474,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":95122,\"title\":\"3,2,1 - Cook!\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/goXK22Z5SQjexaaA0NUwVXXFA6g.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"year\":2014,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.22,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":244025,\"title\":\"Glam Slam\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/A8MTzEeWLj4xlD9shg3MuW9mvNW.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"year\":2023,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.21935483870967742,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":212092,\"title\":\"Food Truck Face Off\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/dfVMSlnz61vgxzQl2mLvNHTFJ65.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"year\":2022,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.2189873417721519,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":244587,\"title\":\"Dinner Time Live with David Chang\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/6isaKyEbUyTlks7eWxTwfAUpXA3.jpg\",\"rating\":6.8,\"year\":2024,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.2169811320754717,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":94913,\"title\":\"Nailed It! France\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/r5Yc9e2bntNNDJBrktij4b9yVu3.jpg\",\"rating\":6,\"year\":2019,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.21607142857142858,\"_genreOverlap\":1}],\"seasonNumber\":24,\"seasonName\":\"Celebrity Edition\",\"seasonOverview\":\"Chef Anne Burrell and Jeff Mauro host a star-studded season of Worst Cooks in America Celebrity Edition with a funky-fresh batch of recruits who dominated Hollywood and won hearts in the '90s. But when it comes to cooking, these stars are totally buggin'.\",\"seasonPoster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/funCeOxM9dQTHIF6C7vyJXl4yLj.jpg\",\"seasonAirDate\":\"2022-04-24\",\"episodes\":[{\"number\":1,\"name\":\"That's So '90s: The Fresh Chefs of Boot Camp\",\"overview\":\"Chef Anne Burrell and co-host Jeff Mauro welcome a fresh batch of celebrity recruits to culinary boot camp, hoping to take these '90s stars from culinary duds to all that and a bag of chips in the kitchen. In order to choose their teams, the chefs need the 411 on what these recruits can and can't do in the kitchen, so Anne and Jeff ask the celebrities to cook a potluck dish. For the main dish challenge, the recruits have to make elevated versions of classic TV dinners, and the chefs decide which dishes deserve to be syndicated and which recruits should be cancelled from the competition.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2022-04-24\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":2,\"name\":\"That's So '90s: Clueless in the Kitchen\",\"overview\":\"Boot camp is transformed into Hollywood Stars, a '90s-style game show where the celebs must put their culinary skills and knowledge to the test. The winning team gains an advantage for the skill drill challenge, where the celebs must create their own spin on avocado toast. Things get fancy for the main dish challenge when mentors Anne Burrell and Jeff Mauro teach their teams how to prepare Steak Oscar. The recruits with the least successful plates must compete in a blind elimination challenge and make unique crostini. Anne and Jeff decide which star's dish doesn't shine as bright as the other.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2022-05-01\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":3,\"name\":\"That's So '90s: Cross-Country Cooking\",\"overview\":\"It's time for the celebs to shred some serious gnar when they discover boot camp has been transformed into WC Peaks, a winter chalet. The recruits compete in a series of winter-inspired culinary games, and then mentors Anne Burrell and Jeff Mauro task the recruits with making a classic apres-ski snack, loaded waffles. In the main dish challenge, the chefs demonstrate classic European schnitzel with potato sides. The two recruits with the least successful dishes must compete in the blind elimination challenge and attempt to cook their way into another week of boot camp.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2022-05-08\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":4,\"name\":\"That's So '90s: Going Coco-Nuts\",\"overview\":\"Chef-mentors Anne Burrell and Jeff Mauro send their recruits on a tropical adventure by playing Legends of the Hidden Coconut. It's a race to please the island gods as the celebs must solve a recipe puzzle and then cook coconut shrimp and a dipping sauce. Then things get fishy in the main dish challenge when the celebs learn how to make seafood curry dishes. While some of the recruits crush the curry game, the two celebs with the worst dishes must compete in the blind elimination challenge.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2022-05-15\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":5,\"name\":\"That's So '90s: Baking Me Crazy\",\"overview\":\"The celebs find boot camp transformed into a colorful, retro diner, and chefs Anne Burrell and Jeff Mauro challenge them to tackle diner favorites like burgers, fries and milkshakes. First, the recruits must determine the flavors in various milkshakes and then retrieve those flavors in a gigantic bowl of sprinkles. Then, the celebs have to make a loaded burger and fries in a fast-paced, tag-team cooking relay. The main dish challenge is stuffed with flavor when Anne and Jeff teach the recruits how to make fruit-filled pastry pockets. Some recruits successfully embrace the sweeter side of boot camp while the bottom two recruits compete in the blind elimination challenge and one is eliminated.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2022-05-15\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"That's So '90s: Saved by the Dough\",\"overview\":\"The celebrities are used to being superstars, but now they have to be superheroes in the kitchen! Chefs Anne Burrell and Jeff Mauro don their own superhero suits to make the recruits complete an obstacle course in order to unlock clues and retrieve a mystery dish to recreate. For the main dish challenge, the recruits tackle an \\\"im-pasta-ble\\\" mission of making fresh pasta and sauce from scratch. Unfortunately, some recruits' superpowers shine brighter than others, and the bottom two recruits must compete in the blind elimination challenge.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2022-05-22\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":7,\"name\":\"That's So '90s: From Worst to First\",\"overview\":\"To start off the final week in boot camp, the remaining celebs play Ravenous Ravenous Recruits, using grabbers to retrieve ingredient balls from a ball pit. For the final skill drill cook, it's every recruit for themselves to create a composed dish using assigned ingredients. Chefs Anne Burrell and Jeff Mauro teach their final two recruits how to make a three-course, restaurant-quality meal, and the finalists put all their culinary skills on display to impress a panel of culinary experts. Judges Ilan Hall, Nilou Motamed and Ayesha Nurdjaja evaluate the recruits' dishes in a blind taste test and determine the winner of the $25,000 prize to charity.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2022-05-29\",\"runtime\":45}],\"firstAirDate\":\"2010-01-03\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}